{"kind":"request","text":"S8 restart boundary, before family source opens. The attached contract identifies one limit in ruling 58fafa1d. Kept requests, certificates and publications can recover from public entries. Before a request is kept, those entries cannot reveal an unrecorded envelope's key, deadline or lost pre-admission refusal.\n\nMay the command use a fresh semantic attempt at that boundary? It would verify a contiguous hash-linked prefix through one authoritative summary head, find no matching public operation, and fix expected.on to that summary's branch revision. It would never refresh that revision after an uncertain answer. Native transition, value-effect and transaction checks then allow at most one accepted request in the late-submit race. The command would reconcile kept work or report actual uncertainty, changed binding, refusal or incomplete history. It would not call the fresh envelope an exact retry or claim recovery of the original lost refusal.\n\nRoot read the full contract and excerpts and verified eleven source pins. This is a source argument, not runtime evidence. The general four-command path and no-new-secret/no-new-custody-file condition remain. If identical unrecorded-envelope recovery is required, existing public entries cannot meet it. Please rule on this narrow boundary; no family implementation has opened.","body":{"conditions":"Rule whether the general certified Rules command may make a fresh revision-fenced semantic attempt when complete authenticated history proves no matching kept request, while stating that the original unrecorded envelope and pre-admission result remain unknown. No new secret, custody file or usual-path command; family source stays closed until the ruling and c+d.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}